WEBVTT

00:16:29.454 --> 00:16:32.496
We had a little bit of adversity losing
our parents relatively early.

00:16:32.537 --> 00:16:34.746
We were fortunate in that
we had our grandparents

00:16:34.746 --> 00:16:37.329
because we were at risk of going
into the foster care system.

00:16:37.787 --> 00:16:41.829
But my grandparents stepped in and they
were amazing, particularly my grandmother.

00:16:41.871 --> 00:16:44.537
She was everything. Unfortunately,
she passed from cancer.

00:16:44.954 --> 00:16:48.954
From that moment on, I literally started
taking care of myself when

00:16:48.954 --> 00:16:49.954
I was 16 years old.

00:16:50.329 --> 00:16:52.746
But Mandela wasn't just taking
care of himself.

00:16:53.246 --> 00:16:55.454
He also had his younger
brother to look after.

00:16:55.704 --> 00:16:57.787
I had a younger brother who
was 14 at the time where

00:16:57.787 --> 00:16:59.162
I essentially had to become his parent.

00:16:59.704 --> 00:17:02.121
And then I started to think
about things that